<title>USA: American Radio says to buy Boston station.</title>
<headline>American Radio says to buy Boston station.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Radio Systems Corp said Friday it has reached an agreement to buy radio station WNFT-AM in Boston from the privately-held Greater Media Inc for about $4.5 million.</p>
<p>American Radio Systems owns six stations in the Boston/Worcester area:  WBMX-FM, WRKO-AM, WEEI-AM, WEGQ-FM, WAAF-FM and WWTM-AM.</p>
<p>The company said the deal is subject to regulatory approval.</p>
